TPC-H-shaped retail CPU configurations
======================================

Every retail source exposes default, par, par_radix, par_built_hash,
par_built_radix, radix, radix_retained, no-reduce, transfer, le, le_runs, and
advised. The par_built_* pair compares parallel hash and eligible RadixRun
providers under identical explicit host-index materialization. Kernel and
full-query shells also retain the sequential built_hash/built_radix comparison.
Standalone/staged runners use standalone_configs! and compile the entire authored
runner for each configuration; the same CQ is not copied between configurations.
Only advised applies stage-local query! advice. Transfer applies
cq_planners::order(transfer) independently to each authored CQ stage, retaining
the same preprocessing, materialization, aggregate heads, and answer contracts.
Most advice follows experiments/gpu/tpch/src/advice.rs; H05 retains its CPU
cycle-closing order and H09 its connected Part-first written order.
See tpch-methodology.txt for pipeline, timing, and correctness semantics.

For a matched parallel provider comparison, run from this directory:

  RAYON_NUM_THREADS=16 cargo xtask bench --tpch --sf 1 --runs 5 \
    --query retail_h09 --config par_built_hash,par_built_radix

Repeat with RAYON_NUM_THREADS=1 for a single-worker control. Archive reports
between thread counts: the standard report filenames do not encode pool size.
Times include query-local index builds; these are not prepared-index probe times.

All 29 entries in src/tpch.rs CASES expose default and transfer: 27 retail-derived
cases plus full tpch_q06 and tpch_q19, which retain their own configuration shells.
This inventory is not the complete canonical ordered TPC-H Q1-Q22 suite.
No input projection or cached data schema changes are needed for transfer.
The historical validation table below does not report transfer validation.
Current transfer validation covers all 29 cases at SF0.1 and SF1, with exact
DuckDB witnesses and separate deterministic counters. See
experiments/gpu/compare/rpt-repair/summary.json from the repository root for the full
matrix, H09 timeout control, paired timing method and remaining limitations.

SF0.1 configuration validation (2026-10-24)
------------------------------------------
Each cell below was exercised with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4 and:

  cargo xtask bench --tpch --sf 0.1 --runs 1 --query retail_QUERY --config CONFIG

Run from features/workloads. "exact" means the selected configuration's TSV
correctness column is "pass": exact complete-answer comparison with DuckDB,
including warm, measured, and independently instrumented counter executions.
Raw reports are target/bench/tpch-0.1-retail_QUERY-config-CONFIG.tsv and .json;
command logs are target/bench/config-validation/QUERY-CONFIG.log.
These one-run checks validate answers, not stable performance rankings.

The 26-query GPU comparison suite excludes H14. H14 is additionally checked
here because it remains a standalone CPU catalog query and uses the same macro.
No LE or le_runs configuration was rejected by the planner.

